Enhancement: Add timeouts for request headers and idle connections

rest-server did not limit how long a client may take to send the request
headers, nor how long an idle keep-alive connection is kept open. A client
could hold connections open indefinitely, each costing a goroutine and a file
descriptor, until the server ran out of file descriptors and legitimate
clients were no longer served.

rest-server now closes a connection if the request headers do not arrive
within 30 seconds or if a keep-alive connection is idle for more than two
minutes. The limits are configurable using the new `--read-header-timeout`
and `--idle-timeout` flags; setting a flag to `0` disables that timeout.
Uploads and downloads are not affected by these timeouts.

https://github.com/restic/rest-server/issues/408
